  {
    "schema_version": "1.0",
    "page_id": "topic-17-2",
    "page_path": "/explore/mining/metal-industries/",
    "name": "Metal Industries",
    "level": 2,
    "parent_path": "/explore/mining/",
    "entity_type": "category",
    "address": null,
    "phone": null,
    "email": null,
    "website": null,
    "logo": null,
    "contact_source_ids": [],
    "description": "Iran's metal industries connect mineral extraction with ironmaking, smelting, refining, alloy production, and the manufacture of usable metal products. Steel, copper, aluminum, and zinc follow different production chains, so their output measures require careful interpretation.",
    "tags": ["Metallurgy", "Steel", "Copper", "Aluminum", "Zinc", "Industrial production"],
    "status": null,
    "editorial_status": "ready_for_review",
    "as_of_date": "2026-10-26",
    "created_at": "2026-10-28T11:36:10Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-10-28T11:36:10Z",
    "seo": {
      "title": "Iran's Metal Industries: Production Chains and Materials | Iran, Unfolded",
      "description": "Understand Iran's steel, copper, aluminum, zinc, and alloy industries through their distinct processing stages and carefully defined production data."
    },
    "content": [
      {
        "id": "industrial-map",
        "type": "text",
        "heading": "From a mineral resource to a usable material",
        "content": "Metal industries transform mineral-bearing materials into products whose composition, shape, and performance can be specified. Iran's USGS industry compilation records separate outputs for direct-reduced iron, raw steel, primary aluminum, refined copper, zinc metal, and ferroalloys. These categories describe different stages and materials; they are not interchangeable measures of industrial size. [s1]\n\nThis section follows that distinction. The steel branch explains iron-based production; copper, aluminum, and zinc branches follow their own extraction and refining chains. Industrial alloys and specialty metals address the further question of how composition and processing create particular properties. The branch structure is an editorial guide to those distinctions, rather than a claim that every material follows one production route.",
        "source_ids": ["s1"]
      },
      {
        "id": "steel-chain",
        "type": "text",
        "heading": "Steel: ironmaking is a separate stage",
        "content": "Steelmaking begins with a choice of metallic inputs. In the blast-furnace route, iron ore is reduced to molten iron before processing in a basic oxygen furnace. Another route uses direct-reduced iron, often called sponge iron, as a feed for an electric arc furnace. Recycled steel can also supply an electric arc furnace. The International Renewable Energy Agency distinguishes these pathways because their material and energy requirements differ. [s2]\n\nAn electric arc furnace melts metallic feed; its presence does not by itself mean that production uses only scrap. Direct-reduced iron and other iron units may enter the furnace alongside recycled material. After steelmaking, casting and rolling turn the material into forms suitable for further manufacture. Some finishing operations occur at different sites or companies from the initial steelmaking stage. [s3]\n\nThis matters when reading Iranian production reports. A tonne of direct-reduced iron can subsequently become part of steel output. Adding the two figures would count material at successive stages rather than create a meaningful finished-metal total. The chart below therefore follows one defined intermediate product independently. [s1][s2]",
        "source_ids": ["s1", "s2", "s3"]
      },
      {
        "id": "dri-trend",
        "type": "chart",
        "content": {
          "type": "line",
          "title": "Iran: reported direct-reduced iron production, 2020–2024",
          "dataset_id": "iran-dri-production",
          "x_field": "period_label",
          "series_ids": ["direct-reduced-iron"],
          "x_axis_label": "USGS reporting year",
          "y_axis_label": "Metric tonnes of direct-reduced iron",
          "y_axis_min": 0,
          "show_legend": false,
          "connect_nulls": false,
          "interpretation": "Reported direct-reduced iron output increased in each successive observation. This measures an ironmaking intermediate, not finished steel or capacity utilization. [s1]"
        },
        "source_ids": ["s1"]
      },
      {
        "id": "steel-process-diagram",
        "type": "markdown-mermaid",
        "title": "Two steelmaking pathways",
        "content": "```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n  A[\"Iron ore\"] -->|\"Reduction\"| B[\"Direct-reduced iron\"]\n  B -->|\"Metallic feed\"| D[\"Electric arc furnace\"]\n  C[\"Recycled steel\"] -->|\"Metallic feed\"| D\n  A -->|\"Blast furnace reduction\"| E[\"Molten iron\"]\n  E -->|\"Metallic feed\"| F[\"Basic oxygen furnace\"]\n  D -->|\"Steelmaking output\"| G[\"Crude steel\"]\n  F -->|\"Steelmaking output\"| G\n  G -->|\"Casting and rolling\"| H[\"Steel products\"]\n```",
        "summary": "Arrows identify material-processing relationships in simplified general steelmaking routes. The diagram does not assign facilities, ownership, market shares, or an emissions rating to Iran.",
        "as_of_date": null,
        "source_ids": ["s2", "s3"]
      },
      {
        "id": "nonferrous-chains",
        "type": "text",
        "heading": "Copper and aluminum follow different chains",
        "content": "Copper production commonly begins by concentrating low-grade sulfide ores, followed by smelting and electrolytic refining to obtain copper cathode. Oxidized ores may instead enter an acid-leaching route. Copper's electrical and thermal conductivity, ductility, and corrosion resistance help explain its uses in wiring, electrical equipment, machinery, and construction. These are general metallurgical relationships, not measurements of Iran's domestic end-use shares. [s4]\n\nRefining is also different from making a finished component. Copper cathode can be converted into wire and rod, tubes, sheet, and strip during semi-fabrication; manufacturers then turn those forms into products. Clean production scrap and material recovered after use can return to the chain. This distinction helps readers separate mine output, refined metal, and manufactured goods when comparing industrial claims. [s5]\n\nAluminum begins with another separation: bauxite is refined into alumina before alumina is converted to metal. Refining removes insoluble material and produces bauxite residue, which requires management alongside the useful product. Aluminum ore, alumina, and metal consequently need separate measures, even when they belong to a connected industrial chain. [s6]",
        "source_ids": ["s4", "s5", "s6"]
      },
      {
        "id": "performance-and-environment",
        "type": "text",
        "heading": "What production totals leave unanswered",
        "content": "Output is only one part of industrial performance. A plant's capacity describes its production capability; output describes what it actually made during a defined period. Comparing them requires matching products, reporting periods, and facility coverage. Likewise, a rising intermediate-product series does not establish better product quality, higher profitability, or lower pollution.\n\nEnvironmental comparisons also require more than a furnace label. Worldsteel distinguishes ore-based ironmaking from scrap-based steelmaking and notes their different emissions profiles. The American Iron and Steel Institute identifies electricity supply and upstream metallic inputs as relevant to an electric arc furnace's emissions. These sources explain the questions to ask; they do not establish Iranian plant-level carbon intensities. [s3][s7]\n\nThe most useful reading of Iran's metal industries therefore follows each material through its stages, then asks how energy, feedstock, recycling, and finishing affect the result. Keeping these stages visible makes reported expansion easier to assess and prevents the same material from being mistaken for several separate additions to national production. [s2][s3][s5]",
        "source_ids": ["s2", "s3", "s5", "s7"]
      }
    ],
